  "source": {
    "title": "Limavady Urban District Council minute book, July 1919 - February 1927: \"Declaration of Members declared elected to serve as Urban District Councillors during the 3 years ending January 1923\", signed 30 January 1920 (PRONI LA/46/2/CA/3; Keep note \"LA/46/2/CA/3\", photo #3, counting from 0)",
    "publisher": "Public Record Office of Northern Ireland (Limavady Urban District Council records)",
    "kind": "official",
    "check": "the nine members who signed the declaration of members declared elected, read from the photographed page (the clerk's margin surname and the signature); the votes and any unsuccessful candidates are not in the minute book"
  },
  "partyLabels": "none-recorded",
  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled 15 January 1920. The whole council of nine was elected. The members are those who signed the declaration of members declared elected on 30 January 1920 before the clerk, J. D. Boyd; Robert Douglas signed as chairman. The signatures of Coghlan and Macrory are hard to read (later minutes write Macrory's initials F.S.M. or F.S.H.); Thomas Ferris signed with his mark. The votes are not yet found in the sources searched."
